 Final Numbers 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data: FactSet; Chart: Axios/Matt Phillips Treasury yields are soaring today, with the 30-year Treasury bond climbing to its highest level since 2004, Axios' Matt Phillips reports .

 The selloff started to accelerate after a sizzling early report on the September economy. Wednesday's gain of roughly 0.15 percentage points in the 10-year Treasury yield was the biggest since April 2025, when President Trump's "Liberation Day" tariff announcement rocked markets. This morning, the 30-year yield rose as high as 5.44%, while 10-year Treasury yields hit 5.13%. 
 
